1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,820
This is Source running locally. Let’s create a task. I enter the goal, add a

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:10,340
requirement, and say how we’ll check the result. Source saves it as a Work item.

3
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:15,820
Now I claim it and start a session. Watch the status change from open, to claimed,

4
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:20,060
to in progress. The session gives the work a record of who started it and where

5
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:25,140
it began. This task is a separate UI example; next we’ll run the three-client

6
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:25,940
rehearsal.

7
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:32,795
Here is the rehearsal running against real Git repositories and Source’s API.

8
00:00:32,795 --> 00:00:37,155
The terminal shows output captured from that run, with pauses added so we can

9
00:00:37,155 --> 00:00:41,955
read it. Three scripted clients start from the same commit. One changes the

10
00:00:41,955 --> 00:00:47,635
theme. One updates the documentation. One changes the page size. They claim

11
00:00:47,635 --> 00:00:52,915
separate tasks, start sessions, and submit proposals. Their execution intervals

12
00:00:52,915 --> 00:00:59,235
overlap. Each client also tries to approve its own change. Source returns HTTP

13
00:00:59,235 --> 00:01:04,635
403 for all three. These credentials can contribute code, but they cannot approve

14
00:01:04,635 --> 00:01:04,995
it.

15
00:01:06,917 --> 00:01:11,437
Back in the browser, I open a change from the rehearsal. The page shows the

16
00:01:11,437 --> 00:01:15,677
request and the two commits being compared. Below that are the checks attached

17
00:01:15,677 --> 00:01:20,517
to this proposal. The rehearsal ran the settings test and a Git diff check.

18
00:01:20,517 --> 00:01:25,477
I evaluate the policy again, then scroll to the evidence. Both records are valid.

19
00:01:25,477 --> 00:01:30,477
The decision has its own record and names the approver. In this demo, a script

20
00:01:30,477 --> 00:01:35,237
plays the maintainer. The checks really ran; the human review is simulated.

21
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:42,367
Once the theme change lands, the other proposals have an old base. Source blocks

22
00:01:42,367 --> 00:01:46,607
the stale update without moving the shared branch. The documentation client

23
00:01:46,607 --> 00:01:52,367
rebases and submits a new proposal. The page-size client hits a real conflict:

24
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:57,287
both clients edited the same line in settings dot JSON. The recovery step keeps

25
00:01:57,287 --> 00:02:01,807
the dark theme and sets the page size to twenty. It then reruns the checks and

26
00:02:01,807 --> 00:02:06,407
submits the revised change. Only after the scripted maintainer accepts that

27
00:02:06,407 --> 00:02:09,007
revision does Source advance the shared branch.

28
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:15,998
Now let’s inspect what landed. I open the repository, switch to History, and

29
00:02:15,998 --> 00:02:20,798
select the page-size commit. The diff shows the change from ten to twenty while

30
00:02:20,798 --> 00:02:26,078
keeping the dark theme. Back in Contents, I open the actual settings file. Both

31
00:02:26,078 --> 00:02:30,478
changes are there. The earlier proposals, their evidence, and their decisions

32
00:02:30,478 --> 00:02:35,598
remain in Source. This is the useful part: we can inspect the final code and

33
00:02:35,598 --> 00:02:37,278
follow the work that produced it.

34
00:02:39,208 --> 00:02:44,688
Source is public and MIT licensed. You can clone it and run both local rehearsals.

35
00:02:44,688 --> 00:02:49,528
Its CI passes, including the PostgreSQL concurrency checks and the two-container

36
00:02:49,528 --> 00:02:54,088
failover test. The Cloudflare path is still a local rehearsal with emulated

37
00:02:54,088 --> 00:02:59,288
Artifacts. We have not verified a deployed Worker or a live Artifacts repository.

38
00:02:59,288 --> 00:03:04,328
That is the next submission gate. For now, this video shows the working local

39
00:03:04,328 --> 00:03:09,848
flow: create work, submit changes, check evidence, recover from a conflict,

40
00:03:09,848 --> 00:03:11,288
and inspect the result.
